  "term": "stress test",
  "definition": "A stress test is a clinical screening tool that puts a person through a demanding task or condition to help reveal problems that may not be obvious at rest. It is used as an indirect way to gauge reserve, meaning the physiological capacity a person can draw on in challenging situations.",
